1. Overview & Purpose
FitLog v2.1 is a zero-dependency, single-page web application (SPA) that runs entirely in the browser. It was designed around one core principle: a user should be able to open a single HTML file and immediately begin tracking their fitness journey — no account, no installation, no backend server required.
The application integrates Google Gemini AI to deliver experiences that would traditionally require a server-side system: natural-language meal parsing, photo-based body-fat estimation, AI-generated multi-week workout plans, and per-day plan regeneration on demand.
FitLog v2.1 is the second major iteration of the project and introduces a production-grade Workout Studio (with plan preview, edit mode, exercise picker, and a full-screen active workout mode), a streak-freeze system, Google Fit and Mi Band BLE integration, cloud sync via a sync-code mechanism, and Progressive Web App support for installability on mobile and desktop devices.

