12. User Interface & Theming
Design Language
FitLog uses a glass-morphism design language: semi-transparent cards with blurred backgrounds and subtle borders, layered on a deep dark (#060812) base. The accent colour is a vibrant teal (#00E5BB) that signals interactive elements, progress indicators, and the brand identity.
Dark / Light Themes
Toggling the theme applies a data-theme attribute to the <body> element. CSS custom properties defined under [data-theme="dark"] and [data-theme="light"] switch the full colour palette without a page reload. The preference is persisted in localStorage and restored on next visit.
CSS Custom Properties
All colours and spacings are defined as CSS custom properties (variables), making global theming changes trivial. Key properties include:
•	--accent-primary: Main teal (#00E5BB)
•	--accent-secondary: Coral/orange accent for warnings
•	--glass-bg: Card background (rgba with backdrop-filter: blur)
•	--glass-border: Subtle card border
•	--text-primary / --text-secondary: Content text colours
Navigation
The top navigation bar contains the FitLog brand logo (inline PNG, base64-encoded), a streak display, and the ⚙️ Settings icon. The bottom navigation provides tab buttons for Dashboard, Nutrition, Workout, Metrics, and Progress.
Responsive Design
The layout is fully responsive using CSS Flexbox and Grid. Cards stack vertically on narrow viewports. The Active Workout Mode uses a full-viewport fixed layout for immersive focus. The rest-timer overlay uses an SVG ring animation centred on screen.

13. Data Storage Architecture
All application data is persisted in the browser's localStorage as JSON strings. There is no IndexedDB, no cookies, and no remote database. The following logical data stores are used:
localStorage Key (conceptual)	Contents
fitlog_nutrition_log	Array of daily nutrition entries: date, meal name, calories, protein, carbs, fat
fitlog_workouts	Array of completed workout sessions: date, exercises, sets, reps, duration
fitlog_active_plan	Current AI workout plan: weeks, days, exercises, current position
fitlog_body_metrics	Array of body measurement entries: date, weight, body fat %
fitlog_hydration	Daily water intake log
fitlog_steps	Daily step count entries
fitlog_streak	Current streak count, freeze count, last active date
fitlog_custom_foods	User-created custom food entries
fitlog_favorites	Favourite food items for quick logging
fitlog_gemini_key	Encrypted Gemini API key
fitlog_theme	User's last selected theme (dark/light)
fitlog_sync_code	Cloud sync code for backup/restore
fitlog_onboarded	Boolean — whether onboarding has been dismissed

localStorage has a per-origin limit of approximately 5–10 MB depending on the browser. Heavy users (years of daily entries) are unlikely to approach this limit given the compact JSON format used.
💡  Data Portability Tip
Use Settings > ☁️ Cloud Sync > 💾 Export JSON at any time to download a full snapshot of your data. This JSON file can be imported into a spreadsheet or used as an offline backup.
The Clear All Data button in the Danger Zone of Settings permanently erases all localStorage data for the FitLog origin. This action is irreversible.


