17. Privacy & Security
Data Residency
All user data — workout logs, nutrition entries, body metrics, and preferences — resides exclusively in the user's own browser localStorage. FitLog's author has no access to this data.
External Data Transmissions
FitLog transmits data to third-party services only in the following explicitly user-initiated scenarios:
•	Google Gemini API — when the user invokes any AI feature (meal logging, workout generation, photo analysis). Data sent: the prompt text and/or base64-encoded image. The Gemini API key is included in the request header.
•	Open Food Facts API — when the user scans a barcode or searches for a food by name. Data sent: the barcode string or search query. No user identity is transmitted.
•	Google Fit API — when the user is signed in with Google Fit and taps Sync Now. Data sent: fitness metrics (steps, weight, calories) to and from Google's servers, governed by Google's own privacy policy.
•	Cloud Sync service — when the user explicitly clicks Backup Now or Restore. Data sent: the full localStorage JSON payload.
API Key Storage
The Gemini API key is stored in localStorage. It is not obfuscated or encrypted beyond the browser's own same-origin isolation. Users should treat it as a sensitive credential.
No Tracking, No Analytics
FitLog does not include any analytics libraries, tracking pixels, or telemetry scripts. There are no third-party advertising or behavioural tracking integrations.

