19. Known Limitations & Roadmap
Current Limitations
•	localStorage size cap (~5 MB): Long-term users with years of daily entries may eventually approach the browser's storage limit. A future migration to IndexedDB would provide significantly more headroom.
•	Gemini API quota: The free tier of the Gemini API has per-minute and per-day call limits. Heavy AI usage (repeated regeneration of workout plans, frequent photo analysis) may result in temporary quota errors.
•	Web Bluetooth (BLE): Not supported in Firefox or Safari. Mi Band connectivity is limited to Chromium-based browsers.
•	Offline AI: All Gemini AI calls require an internet connection. The app works offline for data review and manual logging, but AI features are unavailable without connectivity.
•	Multi-user: FitLog has no user account system. All data belongs to the single browser profile using the app.
•	Accessibility: Full ARIA landmark roles, focus management in modals, and screen-reader-optimised flows are incomplete.
•	Calorie burn estimation: The calories-burned figure on the Dashboard is an estimate based on TDEE and workout duration, not a direct measurement.
Potential Roadmap Items
•	IndexedDB migration for larger data capacity.
•	Export to CSV for nutrition and workout data.
•	Configurable macro goals and daily calorie targets.
•	Notification scheduler for workout reminders.
•	Social sharing of streaks and milestones.
•	Full WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility audit and remediation.
•	Additional AI models (e.g. Claude, GPT-4) as user-selectable backends.
•	Expanded exercise GIF library with muscle-group diagrams.

